# Shell scripts must keep LF endings everywhere.
#
# Git on Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which would check these out
# with CRLF -- and a shell script with \r line endings fails in confusing ways
# ("command not found" on a line that looks fine).  This matters for anyone
# cloning on Windows, not just for CI.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.sh.example text eol=lf
Makefile text eol=lf
.gitattributes text eol=lf

# generated bundles are shell too
dist/* text eol=lf

# docs can follow the platform
*.md text
